        -:   48:
        -:   49:// An awaitable_thread represents a thread-of-execution that is composed of one
        -:   50:// or more "stack frames", with each frame represented by an awaitable_frame.
        -:   51:// All execution occurs in the context of the awaitable_thread's executor. An
        -:   52:// awaitable_thread continues to "pump" the stack frames by repeatedly resuming
        -:   53:// the top stack frame until the stack is empty, or until ownership of the
        -:   54:// stack is transferred to another awaitable_thread object.
        -:   55://
        -:   56://                +------------------------------------+
        -:   57://                | top_of_stack_                      |
        -:   58://                |                                    V
        -:   59:// +--------------+---+                            +-----------------+
        -:   60:// |                  |                            |                 |
        -:   61:// | awaitable_thread |<---------------------------+ awaitable_frame |
        -:   62:// |                  |           attached_thread_ |                 |
        -:   63:// +--------------+---+           (Set only when   +---+-------------+
        -:   64://                |               frames are being     |
        -:   65://                |               actively pumped      | caller_
        -:   66://                |               by a thread, and     |
        -:   67://                |               then only for        V
        -:   68://                |               the top frame.)  +-----------------+
        -:   69://                |                                |                 |
        -:   70://                |                                | awaitable_frame |
        -:   71://                |                                |                 |
        -:   72://                |                                +---+-------------+
        -:   73://                |                                    |
        -:   74://                |                                    | caller_
        -:   75://                |                                    :
        -:   76://                |                                    :
        -:   77://                |                                    |
        -:   78://                |                                    V
        -:   79://                |                                +-----------------+
        -:   80://                | bottom_of_stack_               |                 |
        -:   81://                +------------------------------->| awaitable_frame |
        -:   82://                                                 |                 |
        -:   83://                                                 +-----------------+
        -:   84:
        -:   85:template <typename Executor>
        -:   86:class awaitable_frame_base
